{
  "title": "Flail Chest",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1061/flail-chest",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 23 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "**SUMMARY**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Flail chest is a traumatic chest injury defined as segmental fractures of 3 or more consecutive ribs and is often associated with pulmonary injuries such as hemothorax and pneumothorax.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs of the chest.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment can be nonoperative or operative depending on the presence of respiratory compromise, the number of consecutive rib fractures, and the presence of open fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**EPIDEMIOLOGY**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approximately 300,000 cases per year, 7% require hospitalization for medical and/or surgical treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "greater number of fractured ribs correlates with increased morbidity and mortality",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bimodal distribution",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "younger patients involved in trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "older patients with osteopenia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ribs 7-10** are most commonly fractured",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**ETIOLOGY**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "direct blunt vs penetrating trauma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fracture at the site of impaction or at the angle (i.e. posterolateral bend) of the rib (i.e. biomechanically weakest point)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathologic / metastatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated Injuries",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "medical",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mediastinal injury",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fractures involving ribs 1, 2, or 3 associated with mediastinal injury (aorta or brachial plexus) and worse mortality",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "intra-abdominal organ injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fractures involving **ribs 9 through 12 are associated with intra-abdominal organ injuries (hepatic and splenic most common)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "hemopneumothorax and/or pulmonary contusions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "orthopaedic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scapula fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "clavicle fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**risk for progressive clavicle fracture displacement with ipsilateral upper rib fractures (i.e. ribs 1-4)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**ANATOMY**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "12 pairs of ribs; numbered 1 through 12 according to the corresponding thoracic vertebra to which they are connected posteriorly",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterior ribs articulate with the sternum via the costal cartilage",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "ribs 11-12 are \"floating ribs\" without anterior sternal costal cartilage attachment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Nervous System and Nerves",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "intercostal neurovascular bundle lies posterior-inferiorly adjacent to each rib within the costal groove",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/a05b511b-a1ac-47b5-b503-639fc51d9cce_intercostal_nvb.jpg",
                  "caption": "Neurovascular bundle anatomy"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**PRESENTATION**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "bruising along chest wall",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "respiratory difficulty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "paradoxical respiration",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/img-0201.jpg",
                      "caption": "Flail chest and paradoxical respiration"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "area of injury \"sinks in\" with inspiration, and expands with expiration (opposite of normal chest wall mechanics)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "chest wall deformity can be seen",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/img_0317.jpg",
                      "caption": "Prominent posterior rib fractures"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bony or soft-tissue crepitus is often noted",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**IMAGING**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dedicated rib radiographs are more sensitive (added oblique views and higher energy radiation)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may see associated hemothorax",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/flail%20chest%201b.jpg",
                      "caption": "Flail chest"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensitivity and specificity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "low sensitivity with standard AP and lateral radiographs",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "best modality to assess displacement, segmental injuries, and need for surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "also shows associated thoracic or abdominal injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "sensitivity and specificity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "improved accuracy of diagnosis with CT (vs. radiographs)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**TREATMENT**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no respiratory compromise",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "no flail chest segment (>3 consecutive segmentally fractured ribs)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "supplemental O2 as needed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "incentive spirometry",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "multimodal pain control",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction internal fixation (ORIF)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "displaced rib fractures associated with intractable pain recalcitrant to conservative measures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "flail chest segment (3 or more consecutive ribs with segmental injuries)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "rib fractures associated with failure to wean from a ventilator",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "open rib fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "symptomatic nonunion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "follow Chest Wall Injury Society recommendations for surgical stabilization of rib fractures (SSRF)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/92350c70-3d80-4407-b80e-011614922b08_screenshot_2024-02-27_at_4.10.24_am.jpg",
                          "caption": "SSRF rib fractures algorithm"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "contraindications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hemodynamic instability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "spinal or pelvic fractures that must be stabilized before rib fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "plate and screw constructs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1061/images/img_3580.jpg",
                          "caption": "Plating of rib fractures"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "intramedullary splinting",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "surgical repair of flail chest has been shown to reduce rates of pneumonia, permanent chest deformity, and mortality",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "also shown to reduce the need for tracheostomy, duration of mechanical ventilation, shorter ICU/hospital stays, and overall cost savings",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**Techniques**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**O**pen reduction internal fixation (ORIF)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "lateral thoracotomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "treats anterolateral and posterolateral fractures with lateral decubitus positioning",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "posterior paramedian approach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "treats very posterior rib fractures near costovertebral junction",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "inframammary approach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "treats anterior fracture and costochondral dislocations via supine positioning",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**COMPLICATIONS**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Nonunion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "persistent chest pain >3 months after injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "obtain nonunion workup before fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Intercostal neuralgia**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "avoid injuring the intercostal neurovascular bundle during plating (located posteroinferior to rib)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Periscapular muscle weakness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Pneumonia**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Restrictive type pulmonary function**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "**PROGNOSIS**",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "4",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mortality rate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "as high as 33% when flail chest is present",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "2.5% with surgical stabilization",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
